WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:05.200
Nicole: Let's have a look at some threats
and how they can be protected against.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.810
Abraham: A DoS or denial of service
attack is where a computer is used

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.670
to flood or crash a system due to too
much internet traffic causing them

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.689
to slow down and eventually stop.

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:20.890
This attack can be managed by deploying
firewalls at key points in a network

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.009
to filter out unwanted traffic.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.200
This means that the potential victim
doesn't receive or respond to them.

00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:33.519
Nicole: A DDoS or distributed denial of
service attack involves multiple systems

00:00:33.589 --> 00:00:38.590
orchestrating a synchronised attack to
a single target, overloading a server.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:43.059
These attacks can be seriously
disruptive as the location is difficult

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:46.499
to detect due to the random nature
of the distribution of the attack.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:50.890
This form of attack uses
malicious network traffic packets.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.089
Modern security technologies have
developed to defend against DoS attack,

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:02.510
but the DDoS is more of an elevated threat
and of greater concern to cyber security

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.240
Abraham: Botnet software

00:01:05.969 --> 00:01:09.830
A bot is a piece of malware that
infects a computer to carry out the

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.630
commands of the attacker remotely.

00:01:12.029 --> 00:01:16.690
A botnet is a number of internet connected
devices that are running one or more bots.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:22.130
The attacker controls the botnet to hijack
networks of computers to carry out scams

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.639
and cyberattacks such as data theft,
server crashing and malware distribution.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.670
While botnets can be an attack
in themselves, they can also be

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:33.619
used to execute secondary attacks.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:39.190
Nicole: A trojan is a type of malware
often disguised as legitimate software.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.380
Users are often tricked into loading
and executing trojans on their systems.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:49.080
They enable cyber criminals to
spy and steal sensitive data and

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.130
gain backdoor access to a system.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:57.189
A trojan must be executed by the victim to
gain access to the system via a phishing

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:02.300
or social engineering attack by opening
an infected email or clicking on a link.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.050
This type of threat can be prevented by
not clicking on anything unsolicited.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.320
Abraham: Ransomware is malware
that encrypts and holds a

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.160
victim’s information for ransom.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:18.429
They subsequently cannot access files,
databases or applications and the attacker

00:02:18.429 --> 00:02:20.470
demands a ransom to provide access.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.780
If a system is infected with ransomware
an appropriate decryption tool

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.380
will be needed to regain access.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.890
Antivirus software should be able to
protect systems but also having back

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.589
up data will help in the short term.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.829
Nicole: Spyware is a form of malware
that secretly infects a computer to

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:44.080
gather information such as the sites
visited, usernames, passwords, payment

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.410
information and email activity.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.190
It runs quietly in the
background monitoring activities.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.640
Spyware can enter your computer
through freeware, software bundles

00:02:54.679 --> 00:02:59.350
and phishing and malvertising and
it can also attack smartphones.

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:04.149
If spyware is suspected or to protect
against it a good cybersecurity

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:09.579
program or a robust antivirus software
can be used to clean up the system.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.549
Abraham: Worms are designed to spread from
computer to computer and have the ability

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:16.439
to reproduce themselves to do this.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.430
It operates by inserting itself
into a legitimate programme or

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.780
document that supports macros
in order to execute its code.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.520
To do this it can create
unexpected and damaging effects

00:03:27.559 --> 00:03:29.240
and corrupt or destroy data.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:33.959
It can remain dormant until the
device executes its code and

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.100
once that is infected it can
infect others in the network.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:43.110
It can steal passwords, corrupt files and
spam email contacts amongst other things.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.440
Antivirus software protects against
more than viruses and is an older term.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:51.659
We now tend to refer to it as
antimalware software because it

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.230
protects against all types of
malicious software including viruses.

